<title>FRANCE: Thomson-CSF sells IFF system to Romania.</title>
<headline>Thomson-CSF sells IFF system to Romania.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-03-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>French defence electronics firm Thomson-CSF said on Thursday its Thomson-CSF Communications subsidiary won a contract to supply Identification Friend or Foe (IFF) equipment to the Romanian armed forces.</p>
<p>The contract will be shared with the Romanian Aerostar company, based in Bacau, northern Romania, and includes a technology transfer and creation of a joint venture company.</p>
<p>The IFF system will allow the army, navy and air force to identify aircraft, missiles and vessels, initially in the national mode and can be upgraded to include Nato standards, in the event of accession to Nato. It gave no contract value.</p>
</text>
